character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  胡 | hú | reckless; beard; northern tribes; non-Han | imprudente; barba; pueblos del norte; nómada | 月 | moon / flesh | 月 (flesh / dewlap of animal) | 古 (gǔ, ancient / phonetic) | 9 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic character showing dewlap flesh 月 of oxen; loan character transcribing Mongolian 'hottog' (water well). | Ancient elders (古) stroke their long beards (月) while resting near northern water wells (胡). | Ancianos (古) acarician sus largas barbas (月) junto a los pozos norteños de agua (胡). | 35 | JRB | ""
  同 | tòng | same; alley; together | mismo; callejón; juntos | 口 | mouth | 冂 (enclosure) + 一 (one) | 口 (kǒu, mouth in agreement) | 6 | 半包围结构 | Ideogram showing people speaking with one unified voice under an enclosure; used as phonetic loan for lane in hutong. | Neighbors gather together under one enclosure (冂) to speak with one mouth (口) along the shared alley (同). | Los vecinos se congregan bajo un mismo techo (冂) hablando a una sola voz (口) en el callejón común (同). | 51 | BMR | 衚衕

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Northern travelers (胡) gathered together in agreement (同) around water-well settlements, giving birth to the hutong (胡同).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Los pobladores del norte (胡) se agrupaban juntos (同) junto a los pozos de agua, creando el callejón hutong (胡同).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Linguistically derived from Mongolian 'hottog' (water well) during the Yuan Dynasty (Dadu / Beijing); settlements clustered around wells became narrow communal alleys.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Rising tone followed by falling tone or neutral tone: 'hú tòng' (35-51 or 35-2 in Beijing dialect). Syllable 'tòng' drops firmly, often lightened in vernacular speech.

