semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 胡同 specifically denotes traditional northern Chinese residential alleys bordered by grey-brick courtyard walls.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 胡同 vs. 街道 | jiēdào | 街道 refers broadly to paved city traffic streets with motor vehicles, whereas 胡同 refers to intimate residential alleys formed by courtyard walls.
    2 | 胡同 vs. 弄堂 | lòngtáng | 胡同 is the northern (Beijing) cultural term for lanes, while 弄堂 (or 里弄) specifically describes Shanghai and southern alleyways.
    3 | 胡同 vs. 小巷 | xiǎoxiàng | 小巷 is a generic, literary term for any narrow passage in any city, while 胡同 carries specific historical identity tied to Yuan, Ming, and Qing Beijing.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 老北京的魂，大半凝固在错落有致的胡同里。斑驳的朱漆大门，门口蹲坐着威武的石狮，门墩上雕刻着吉祥的花草纹样。傍晚时分炊烟渐起，一声清脆悠长的鸽哨掠过瓦檐，那是深宅大院里最富有人情味的天伦图景。 | Lǎo Běijīng de hún, dàbàn nínggù zài cuòluò-yǒuzhì de hútòng lǐ. Bānbó de zhūqī dàmén, ménkǒu dūnzuò zhe wēiwǔ de shíshī, méndūn shàng diāokè zhe jíxiáng de huācǎo wényàng. Bàngwǎn shífēn chuīyān jiàn qǐ, yì shēng qīngcuì yōucháng de gēshào lüèguò wǎyán, nà shì shēnzhái-dàyuàn lǐ zuì fùyǒu rénqíngwèi de tiānlún tújǐng. | Old Beijing's soul is set in winding hutongs. Peeling vermilion gates flanked by stone lions and auspicious carvings welcome evening hearth smoke. A crisp pigeon whistle grazes tile eaves, painting a scene rich with human warmth. | El alma de Pekín reposa en sus callejones. Portones bermejos flanqueados por leones de piedra guardan el humo de las cocinas al atardecer. El silbido de las palomas surca los tejados, dibujando una estampa entrañable de convivencia.
  #2 | 在现代城市更新与历史文化名城保护的交汇点上，胡同肌理的修复成了关键课题。市政规划者摒弃大拆大建的粗暴模式，转而推行渐进式的“微循环”改造。在保留原住民市井记忆的同时，完善供暖排污管网，让古老胡同焕发出现代宜居生机。 | Zài xiàndài chéngshì gēngxīn yǔ lìshǐ wénhuà míngchéng bǎohù de jiāohuìdiǎn shàng, hútòng jīlǐ de xiūfù chéng le guānjiàn kètí. Shìzhèng guīhuàzhě bǐngqì dàchāi-dàjiàn de cūbào móshì, zhuǎn'ér tuīxíng jiànjìnxìng de 'wēixúnhuán' gǎizào. Zài bǎoliú yuánzhùmín shìjǐng jìyì de tóngshí, wánshàn gōngnuǎn páiwū guǎnwǎng, ràng gǔlǎo hútòng huànfā chū xiàndài yíjū shēngjī. | Preserving historical cities makes hutong restoration pivotal. Planners abandon demolition for organic micro-renovation. Preserving resident memories while modernizing heating and drainage breathes livable vitality into ancient alleys. | En la renovación urbana, la restauración de los hutongs es crucial. Los urbanistas rechazan el derribo masivo y optan por mejoras graduales. Al renovar saneamientos y calefacción sin desalojar vecinos, los viejos callejones cobran nueva vida.
